<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) (Aves egg shells: Uria aalge (Common Guillemot), Vanellus vanellus (Northern Lapwing), Strix aluco (Tawny Owl), Podiceps cristatus (Great Crested Grebe); 30 auk + penguin species (1389 eggs); 181 species / 30 orders)",
        "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) faithfully reproduces Aves egg shells: Uria aalge (Common Guillemot), Vanellus vanellus (Northern Lapwing), Strix aluco (Tawny Owl), Podiceps cristatus (Great Crested Grebe); 30 auk + penguin species (1389 eggs); 181 species / 30 orders morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Aves egg shells: Uria aalge (Common Guillemot), Vanellus vanellus (Northern Lapwing), Strix aluco (Tawny Owl), Podiceps cristatus (Great Crested Grebe); 30 auk + penguin species (1389 eggs); 181 species / 30 orders specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py> ;
    schema:about "Aves egg shells: Uria aalge (Common Guillemot), Vanellus vanellus (Northern Lapwing), Strix aluco (Tawny Owl), Podiceps cristatus (Great Crested Grebe); 30 auk + penguin species (1389 eggs); 181 species / 30 orders" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Anything about eggshell microstructure, colour, or non-avian hard-shelled eggs beyond Thompson's mention.",
        "does_not_claim: That the oviduct pressure mechanism (Thompson pp. 654-660) is the cause of the family; only the geometric claim is tested.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form volume of the solid of revolution 315 V / (4 pi (L/2)^3) = 105 c0^2 + 21 (c1^2 + 2 c0 c2) + 9 (c2^2 + 2 c1 c3) + 5 c3^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Preston (1953) four-parameter meridian family y = (c0 + c1 x + c2 x^2 + c3 x^3) sqrt(1 - x^2) with Biggins et al. (2018) indices and a closed-form polar asymmetry R_pole = p(+/-1)^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Species-mean elongation table (30 species), 1389-egg morphospace, Deeming PC2 vs relative egg mass Spearman test.",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 652: eggs are simple solids of revolution; forms range from spherical (owl, penguin, tortoise) through ellipsoidal (grebe, cormorant, pelican) and ovoid (hen) to blunt-pointed conical (guillemot, puffin, sandpiper, plover, curlew); prolate never oblate.",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 655 (5): the most unsymmetrical / tapered eggs are large relative to the parent bird.",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 658: envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P.",
        "transfer_boundary: Biggins et al. (2018) eggs are auks and penguins (plus a 10-egg range set); order-level breadth comes only from Deeming's PCs.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Preston family is a 1953 descriptor adopted as the quantitative reading of Thompson's 'definite family'; Thompson himself gave no algebraic family (he rejected Steiner's Cartesian oval)." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py; output: docs/media/t1917_034_on_the_shapes_of_eggs_and_of_c_comparison.png; organism: Aves egg shells: Uria aalge (Common Guillemot), Vanellus vanellus (Northern Lapwing), Strix aluco (Tawny Owl), Podiceps cristatus (Great Crested Grebe); 30 auk + penguin species (1389 eggs); 181 species / 30 orders; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 652: eggs are simple solids of revolution; forms range from spherical (owl, penguin, tortoise) through ellipsoidal (grebe, cormorant, pelican) and ovoid (hen) to blunt-pointed conical (guillemot, puffin, sandpiper, plover, curlew); prolate never oblate. | Thompson 1917 p. 655 (5): the most unsymmetrical / tapered eggs are large relative to the parent bird. | Thompson 1917 p. 658: envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P.; reconstructed_in_script: Preston (1953) four-parameter meridian family y = (c0 + c1 x + c2 x^2 + c3 x^3) sqrt(1 - x^2) with Biggins et al. (2018) indices and a closed-form polar asymmetry R_pole = p(+/-1)^2. | Closed-form volume of the solid of revolution 315 V / (4 pi (L/2)^3) = 105 c0^2 + 21 (c1^2 + 2 c0 c2) + 9 (c2^2 + 2 c1 c3) + 5 c3^2. | Species-mean elongation table (30 species), 1389-egg morphospace, Deeming PC2 vs relative egg mass Spearman test.; transfer_boundary: The Preston family is a 1953 descriptor adopted as the quantitative reading of Thompson's 'definite family'; Thompson himself gave no algebraic family (he rejected Steiner's Cartesian oval). | Biggins et al. (2018) eggs are auks and penguins (plus a 10-egg range set); order-level breadth comes only from Deeming's PCs.; does_not_claim: That the oviduct pressure mechanism (Thompson pp. 654-660) is the cause of the family; only the geometric claim is tested. | Anything about eggshell microstructure, colour, or non-avian hard-shelled eggs beyond Thompson's mention.]; other sources: On Growth and Form (Ch. XV, On the Shapes of Eggs, and of Certain Other Hollow Structures, pp. 652-669) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit-thompson1917-t1917-034-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit-thompson1917-t1917-034-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit-thompson1917-t1917-034-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit-thompson1917-t1917-034-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit-thompson1917-t1917-034-5> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.61e-01 .

