<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Preston Ovoid Meridian: Pole Radii, Symmetric-Ends Criterion and Reflection Invariance of Polar Asymmetry" ;
    dct:description "Defines Thompson's 'definite family' of meridian curves and derives the closed-form polar-asymmetry index PA = max(R_-/R_+, R_+/R_-) that reproduces Biggins et al.'s numerically searched index on all 1389 eggs (Pearson r = 0.99997); the symmetric-ends criterion c1 + c3 = 0 formalises Thompson's grebe / pelican / cormorant class and the sphere member formalises his owl / tortoise class | Variables: x: normalised axial coordinate on [-1, 1] (half-length = 1); y: normalised half-breadth; c0, c1, c2, c3: Preston (1953) coefficients (c0 breadth, c1 / c3 odd asymmetry and pointedness terms, c2 even cylindricity term); R_pole = p(±1)^2: osculating-circle radius at each pole; s = ±1: pole selector" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) p. 652; Preston (1953) Auk 70:160-182; Biggins, Thompson & Birkhead (2018) Ecol. Evol. 8:9728-9738 Eq. (1)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_034.lean#L40-L66>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L46-L70> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def prestonPoly (c0 c1 c2 c3 x : Int) : Int :=
  c0 + c1 * x + c2 * (x * x) + c3 * (x * x * x)
def prestonHalfBreadthSq (c0 c1 c2 c3 x : Int) : Int :=
  prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 x * prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 x * (1 - x * x)
def poleRadius (c0 c1 c2 c3 s : Int) : Int :=
  prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 s * prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 s
theorem preston_pole_asymmetry_criterion (c0 c1 c2 c3 x : Int) :
    prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 1 - prestonPoly c0 c1 c2 c3 (-1) = 2 * (c1 + c3) ∧
    (c1 + c3 = 0 → poleRadius c0 c1 c2 c3 1 = poleRadius c0 c1 c2 c3 (-1)) ∧
    poleRadius c0 (-c1) c2 (-c3) 1 = poleRadius c0 c1 c2 c3 (-1) ∧
    prestonPoly 1 0 0 0 x = 1 ∧
    prestonHalfBreadthSq 1 0 0 0 x + x * x = 1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "y(x) = p(x) sqrt(1 - x^2),  p(x) = c0 + c1 x + c2 x^2 + c3 x^3;  R_pole = p(±1)^2;  p(1) - p(-1) = 2 (c1 + c3);  c1 + c3 = 0 ⇒ R_+ = R_-;  R(c0, -c1, c2, -c3; +1) = R(c0, c1, c2, c3; -1);  p ≡ 1 ⇒ y^2 + x^2 = 1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.prestonPoly" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.preston_pole_asymmetry_criterion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Exact Volume of the Preston Solid of Revolution: Sphere Normalisation, Ellipsoid Breadth-Squared Scaling and End-for-End Reflection Invariance" ;
    dct:description "Makes the 'solid of revolution' part of the claim quantitative: the volume functional of the meridian family in closed form (checked numerically in the script's self-test against trapezoidal integration to 1e-3 on the guillemot C126) and its invariance under reversing which pole is pointed | Variables: V: egg volume; L: egg length (mm); c0..c3: Preston coefficients; the integral ∫_{-1}^{1} p(x)^2 (1 - x^2) dx evaluated exactly term by term (∫ x^{2k}(1 - x^2) dx = 4 / ((2k+1)(2k+3)))" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) p. 652 ('simple solids of revolution'); Biggins et al. (2018) volume computation in Analysis.R (volcc)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_034.lean#L82-L92>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L72-L81> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def prestonVolume315 (c0 c1 c2 c3 : Int) : Int :=
  105 * (c0 * c0) + 21 * (c1 * c1 + 2 * (c0 * c2)) + 9 * (c2 * c2 + 2 * (c1 * c3)) + 5 * (c3 * c3)
theorem preston_volume_sphere_ellipsoid_reflection (c0 c1 c2 c3 : Int) :
    prestonVolume315 1 0 0 0 = 105 ∧
    prestonVolume315 (2 * c0) 0 0 0 = 4 * prestonVolume315 c0 0 0 0 ∧
    prestonVolume315 c0 (-c1) c2 (-c3) = prestonVolume315 c0 c1 c2 c3
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "315 V / (4 π (L/2)^3) = 105 c0^2 + 21 (c1^2 + 2 c0 c2) + 9 (c2^2 + 2 c1 c3) + 5 c3^2;  sphere (c0 = 1) ⇒ 105 ⇒ V = 4π/3;  V(2 c0, 0, 0, 0) = 4 V(c0, 0, 0, 0);  V(c0, -c1, c2, -c3) = V(c0, c1, c2, c3)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.prestonVolume315" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.preston_volume_sphere_ellipsoid_reflection" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson Envelope Equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P at the Poles: Sphere under Uniform Pressure and Pole-Tension Proportional to Pole Radius" ;
    dct:description "Formalises Thompson's p. 658 'equation of all eggs in the universe' in cleared-denominator form, derives the sphere for uniform pressure (p. 659) and shows that under his own pole assumption (pn = 0, one P) the tension is proportional to the pole radius, so his side-remark that T is greatest at the small end has the sign reversed - recorded in the audit as a mixed detail orthogonal to the shape-family claim | Variables: pn: normal component of external (oviduct) pressure; T: membrane tension; r, r': principal radii of curvature; P: internal fluid pressure; R: common pole radius; Rb, Rp: blunt and pointed pole radii" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) pp. 658-659; Thompson (1908) Nature 78:111-113" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_034.lean#L112-L133>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L56-L70> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def laplaceResidual (pn T r r' P : Int) : Int :=
  pn * (r * r') + T * (r + r') - P * (r * r')
def poleTwiceTension (P R : Int) : Int :=
  P * R
theorem thompson_envelope_pole_equilibrium (T R P Rb Rp : Int)
    (hR : R ≠ 0) (hP : 0 < P) (hRb : Rp < Rb) :
    laplaceResidual 0 T R R P = T * (R + R) - P * (R * R) ∧
    (laplaceResidual 0 T R R P = 0 → P * R = 2 * T) ∧
    poleTwiceTension P Rp < poleTwiceTension P Rb
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "pn r r' + T (r + r') - P r r' = 0;  at a pole r = r' = R with pn = 0:  T (R + R) - P R^2 = 0 ⇒ P R = 2 T;  0 < P ∧ Rp < Rb ⇒ P Rp < P Rb (blunt pole carries the larger tension)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.laplaceResidual" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.thompson_envelope_pole_equilibrium" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson Cone-Ended-Cylinder Equilibrium p cos²θ = p' cos²θ': Lower External Pressure at the Tapered End" ;
    dct:description "Thompson's p. 657 force balance for the guillemot-type conical egg in the oviduct; proves the direction he states ('at the more tapered end where θ is small p is small'), which underlies his claim that the pointed form favours blunt-end-first transport (p. 658) | Variables: p, p': radial pressures at the two conical ends; θ, θ': cone semi-angles (θ small at the tapered end); a, a': integer-scaled cos^2 of the semi-angles (N a common scale); the tapered end has the larger cos^2" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) pp. 657-658" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_034.lean#L147-L161>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L56-L70> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def coneBalance (p a p' a' : Int) : Prop :=
  p * a = p' * a'
theorem thompson_cone_equilibrium_tapered_end_low_pressure (p a p' a' : Int)
    (hbal : coneBalance p a p' a') (ha : 0 ≤ a) (hp' : 0 < p') (hlt : a' < a) :
    p < p'
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p a = p' a' with a = N cos^2(θ), a' = N cos^2(θ');  0 ≤ a ∧ 0 < p' ∧ a' < a ⇒ p < p'" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.coneBalance" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.thompson_cone_equilibrium_tapered_end_low_pressure" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-034-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Prolate-Never-Oblate: Elongation ≥ 1 and Mid-Point Maximum Breadth of the Ellipsoid Member" ;
    dct:description "Formalises Thompson's p. 652 statement that the egg 'is a prolate, but never an oblate, spheroid' for the ellipsoid member of the family; the script tests it empirically as min Elongation = 1.035 over 1399 eggs | Variables: B: maximum breadth; L: length; k: half-length scale (pixels or mm); c0: ellipsoid breadth coefficient (Elongation E = L/B = 1/c0); x: normalised axial coordinate" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) p. 652" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_034.lean#L173-L191>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/83b41df2a/thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py#L56-L70> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ellipsoidBreadth (c0 k : Int) : Int :=
  2 * (c0 * k)
def ellipsoidLength (k : Int) : Int :=
  2 * k
theorem thompson_prolate_never_oblate_ellipsoid (c0 k x : Int)
    (hc : c0 ≤ 1) (hk : 0 ≤ k) (hx : 0 ≤ x * x) (hc0 : 0 ≤ c0 * c0) :
    ellipsoidBreadth c0 k ≤ ellipsoidLength k ∧
    prestonHalfBreadthSq c0 0 0 0 x ≤ c0 * c0 ∧
    prestonHalfBreadthSq c0 0 0 0 0 = c0 * c0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "B = 2 c0 k,  L = 2 k;  c0 ≤ 1 ∧ 0 ≤ k ⇒ B ≤ L;  c0^2 (1 - x^2) ≤ c0^2 for x^2 ≥ 0;  y(0)^2 = c0^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/ece3.4412>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/078111a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/jav.01528>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aaj1945>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/4081145>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.8kv2b20>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.q8rp3> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Geometric: Preston (1953) four-parameter ovoid family of meridian curves for egg solids of revolution, closed by Thompson's (1917) envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.ellipsoidBreadth" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_228.thompson_prolate_never_oblate_ellipsoid" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

